{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "041K", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$Z' \\to Z$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$f : X \\to Z$", "MATH_0004": "$f' : Z' \\times_Z X \\to Z'$", "MATH_0005": "$X'$", "MATH_0006": "$Z' \\times_Z X$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\varphi : X' \\times_Z Z' \\longrightarrow Z' \\times_Z X'\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$Z' \\times_Z Z' \\times_Z X$", "MATH_0009": "$X'/Z'/Z$", "MATH_0010": "$X' \\to Z'$", "MATH_0011": "$Y \\to Z$", "MATH_0012": "$Z$", "MATH_0013": "$\\psi : Z' \\times_Z Y \\to X'$", "MATH_0014": "$Y \\to Z$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{Y} = \\{Z' \\times_Z Y \\to Y\\}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\psi$", "MATH_0017": "$X(Z' \\times_Z Y)$", "MATH_0018": "$\\psi \\in \\check{H}^0(\\mathcal{Y}, X)$", "MATH_0019": "$X$", "MATH_0020": "$Y \\to X$", "MATH_0021": "$Z'$", "MATH_0022": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties-morphisms}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-quasi-affine-local}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{descent-definition-descent-datum}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{descent-lemma-descent-data-sheaves}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{descent-lemma-quasi-affine}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{descent-lemma-descending-property-quasi-affine}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{spaces-properties-proposition-sheaf-fpqc}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-isomorphism}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ab7b7bca0e5be52a812dad2444e592a71d8c257d6af0d960b8947fd46f3e6f56", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:68b92673e1aec1b66526bf6985ba1a03b5b7b599df9f6da7a4874ee7b3ab8775", "source_text": "We will use\nLemma <REF_0001>\nto prove this. Assumptions (1) and (2) of that lemma follow from\nMorphisms of Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0001> be a surjective flat morphism of affine schemes over <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a morphism of algebraic spaces, and assume\nthat the base change <MATH_0004> is quasi-affine.\nLet <MATH_0005> be a scheme representing <MATH_0006>.\nWe obtain a canonical isomorphism\n<MATH_0007>\nsince both schemes represent the algebraic space <MATH_0008>.\nThis is a descent datum for <MATH_0009>, see\nDescent, Definition <REF_0003>\n(verification omitted, compare with\nDescent, Lemma <REF_0004>).\nSince <MATH_0010> is quasi-affine this descent datum is effective, see\nDescent, Lemma <REF_0005>.\nThus there exists a scheme <MATH_0011> over <MATH_0012> and an\nisomorphism <MATH_0013> compatible with descent data.\nOf course <MATH_0014> is quasi-affine (by construction or by\nDescent, Lemma <REF_0006>).\nNote that <MATH_0015> is a\nfpqc covering, and interpreting <MATH_0016> as an element of\n<MATH_0017> we see that <MATH_0018>.\nBy the sheaf condition for <MATH_0019> (see\nProperties of Spaces, Proposition\n<REF_0007>)\nwe obtain a morphism <MATH_0020>.\nBy construction the base change of this to <MATH_0021> is an isomorphism, hence\nan isomorphism by\nLemma <REF_0008>.\nThis proves that <MATH_0022> is representable by a quasi-affine scheme and we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1cf8d0d532b12a0b735cd0edd26bc6690c8e6eec060b9c728572273a20c9a918", "unit_id": "tag:0423:proof"}
